{"id":"word:hebrew:H6160","type":"word","title":"עֲרָבָה","subtitle":"H6160 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a desert ; especially (with the article prefix) the (generally) sterile valley of the Jordan and its continuation to the Red Sea","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to עֲרָבָה (H6160) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 61 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"עֲרָבָה (ʻărâbâh) means a desert ; especially (with the article prefix) the (generally) sterile valley of the Jordan and its continuation to the Red Sea First listed occurrence: 1Sam 23 24."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"עֲרָבָה","transliteration":"ʻărâbâh","pronunciation":"ar-aw-baw'","strong":"H6160","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6160","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["בְּ/עַֽרְבֹ֣ת","הָ/עֲרָבָֽה","בְּ/עַֽרְב֣וֹת","הָ/עֲרָבָ֑ה","בָּ/עֲרָבָ֔ה"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncfsa",17],["HR/Ncfpc",17],["HRd/Ncfsa",11],["HNcfsa",4],["HC/Td/Ncfsa",2],["HC/Ncfsa",2],["HNcfpc",2],["HC/Rd/Ncfsa",2],["HC/Ncfsc/Sp3fs",1],["HNcfpa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a desert ; especially (with the article prefix) the (generally) sterile valley of the Jordan and its continuation to the Red Sea","usage":"Arabah, champaign, desert, evening, heaven, plain, wilderness. See also 1026 .","full":"H6160. arabah I. עֲרָבָה 61 noun feminine desert-plain, steppe ; — absolute ׳ע 2Sam 4:7 +, suffix עַרְבָתָהּ Isa 51:3 ; plural עֲרָבוֺת Jer 5:6 ; Psa 68:5 , construct עַרְבוֺת 2Kin 25:5 +, עַרְבֹת Jer 52:8 ; &#8212; 1 earliest use: a. arid steppe west of Dead Sea (in southern Judah) 1Sam 23:24 , also Ezek 47:8 ; Isa 51:3 , whence name הָע ׳יָם Josh 3:16 (JE) || הַמֶּלַח יָם ), also 2Kin 14:25 ; Deut 4:49 , and (|| id .) 3:17 ; Josh 12:3 (D); הָעֲרָבָה נַחַל Amos 6:14 must be east of Dead Sea, si vera lectio, but read probably ׳נ מִצְרַיִם see נַחַל . b. Jordan-valley west of river + adjacent plain ; near ford (opposite Jericho) 2Sam 2:29 , compare Josh 8:14 (JE); also Deut 11:30 ; 2Kin 25:4 = Jer 39:4 = 52:7 ; &#8212; 2Sam 15:28 ; 17:16 see עֲבָרָה c. Jordan-valley east of river 2Sam 4:7 . 2 in D: a. especially of east Jordan plain Deut 1:1 (probably) Josh 12:1 , 3 , east half of Jordan-valley Deut 3:17 ; 4:49 ; of entire Jordan-valley (between כִּנֶּרֶת and Dead Sea, modern El-Ghôr, the Depression ) 1:7 ; Josh 11:2 , 16 ; west Jordan plain only 12:8 ; depression south of Dead Sea (modern Wady el-`Arabah ) Deut 2:8 . 3 in P always plural construct מוֺאָב עַרְבוֺת (east Jordan) Num 22:1 11 t. (see מוֺאָב ); ׳ע עְרֵחוֺ (West Jordan) Josh 4:13 ; 5:10 , also 2Kin 25:5 = Jer 39:5 = 52:8 . 4 apparently North Arabian desert Isa 40:3 ; 41:19 . 5 in General the steppe (often || מִדְבָּר ), Jer 17:6 ; 50:12 ; Isa 33:9 ; 35:1 , 6 ; Job 24:5 ; 39:6 ; Psa 68:5 ; עֲרָבוֺת זְאֵב Jer 5:6 (figurative of invader); compare description of Exodus וְשׁוּחָה עֲרָבָה אֶרֶץ 2:6 ; in simile, of a plain , of future land of Judah Zech 14:10 . &#8212; See Dr Deut 1:1 and references Buhl Geogr. 111 . עַרְבָתִי see הָעֲרָבָה בֵּית V. ערב (√ of following; compare Assyrian erêbu , enter, go in ; erêb šamši , sunset ; Arabic set (distinct from depart , = Sabean עֿרב withdraw , according to DHM Epigr. Denkm. 27 ), place of sunset, west ; Sabean מערבי מערבם, [not עֿ !] west, western , CIS iv. p. 199 DHM l.c .; Ethiopic set (of heavenly bodies), so Syriac ; evening (Lag BN 64 f. ); Zinjirli מערב west ; Late Hebrew עֶרֶב = Biblical Hebrew. Hence also Εὐπώπη , Europe , Lewy Fremdw. 139 ).","rootNote":"from 6150 (in the sense of sterility);","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 23 24","keyReferences":["1Sam 23 24","2Kgs 14 25","2Kgs 25 4","2Kgs 25 5","2Sam 2 29","2Sam 4 7","2Sam 15 28","2Sam 17 16"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":61,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 23 24","book":"1Sam","chap